  "inShort": "The project is behind on verifiable progress. The final devlog reports a finished level, but no playable artifact was shown, so completed game work remains unknown. The main gap is an accessible build: neither linked media item shows the game.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hf200z5xoz8qjmdfvfi",
      "text": "A public repository of the Godot demo projects the game builds on remains done. The inspected repository contains Godot demos and import instructions, not this game's playable level."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hff00z6xoz88svm5zwp",
      "text": "An animated reference video for the art style remains done. Its inspected title and thumbnail provide a cartoon visual reference; the animation was not viewed. Reusing the film link this sprint does not show the game's jump or level."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hfy00z7xoz83i3lhw8g",
      "text": "A reference article on what playtesting is, for the team to read remains done. The inspected article explains playtesting, but does not document anyone testing this build."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hgb00z8xoz82dr7tqni",
      "text": "A private design board for the team remains done through its attached artifact. No inspection findings or new board evidence were supplied this sprint."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The final devlog reports a complete level, collectibles, enemies and an ending. That would move the checkpoint goal, despite sitting outside the listed tasks. However, no build or itch.io link accompanies it. The image caption describes a jumping gnome, but the image shows mountains. The video title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny, not gameplay."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What accessible evidence supports the reported playable jump and completed first level?",
    "What did the reported second-pit playtest establish about the controls, beyond repeated falls?"
  ],
  "direction": {
    "goal": {
      "value": "stalled",
      "why": "The completion report adds no inspectable game evidence beyond last sprint's unsupported playtest report."
    },
    "stage": {
      "value": "stalled",
      "why": "The sprint adds no inspectable evidence that the core works or that the game's style is chosen."
    }
  },
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #4 announces completion and itch.io availability, with 0 applause and 0 views; the project provides no playable destination link.",
    "team": "Alex's stated 10–15 hours weekly gives 40–60 hours across the checkpoint, now over. Mia stopped confirming work after week one, so her unstated capacity cannot support expectations for implementation or testing.",
    "management": "The retained tasks are closed, but they cover references and a board rather than the playable goal; two consecutive sprints added claims without inspectable game evidence. The prototype-devlog requirement is satisfied, but that administrative progress does not demonstrate the core or move toward a release people can play."
  }
}

